@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About — MiniLeague Baseball</PageTitle>

@* Keep this in step with the "Data, credits and disclaimer" part of README.md and wwwroot/data/ATTRIBUTION.md. *@
<div class="about-page" data-testid="about">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Class="mb-1">About MiniLeague Baseball</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mud-text-secondary mb-4">
        Historical baseball simulation powered by public historical statistics. Pick a classic team,
        manage the game and watch it play out on the real numbers.
    </MudText>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-4" Elevation="1" data-testid="about-disclaimer">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mb-2"><b>Disclaimer</b></MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            MiniLeague Baseball is an independent fan project. It is not affiliated with, authorized by or endorsed by
            Major League Baseball, the Major League Baseball Players Association, or any club.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            Team, player and ballpark names appear only to identify the historical teams and players whose published
            statistics the game uses. All trademarks and names belong to their owners. The game uses no team or league
            logos, and the players you see on the field are generic figures, not likenesses of real people.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-4" Elevation="1" data-testid="about-data">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mb-2"><b>Statistics and data</b></MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            Player and team statistics come from the
            <MudLink Href="https://sabr.org/lahman-database/" Target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lahman Baseball Database</MudLink>
            by Sean Lahman, used under the
            <MudLink Href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" Target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 license (CC BY-SA 3.0)</MudLink>.
            The team data in this game was generated from it and is shared under the same license.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            From Lahman: batting and pitching lines, fielding ratings (range, errors and arm, measured against the
            league average at each position that season), each season's league error and strikeout rates, and each
            ballpark's overall scoring factor.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Not from Lahman: the fence distances and wall heights of the ballparks were entered by hand from memory of
            the real parks and are approximate.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-4" Elevation="1" data-testid="about-music">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mb-2"><b>Organ music</b></MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            The organ tunes are public-domain compositions: <em>Take Me Out to the Ball Game</em> (Albert Von Tilzer,
            1908), <em>La Raspa</em> (traditional), <em>Hail to the Chief</em> (James Sanderson, 1812), Chopin's
            <em>Funeral March</em> and the traditional cavalry charge call. All sounds are made in your browser.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Elevation="1" data-testid="about-code">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mb-2"><b>Source code</b></MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            The game's code is open source under the MIT License and lives on
            <MudLink Href="https://github.com/josemoliver/MiniLeagueBaseball" Target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</MudLink>.
            Version @AppVersion.Current.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
</div>
